# Copy this file to `.env` (which is git-ignored) and uncomment / fill in
# whichever overrides you need. All variables that start with EXPO_PUBLIC_
# get inlined into the JS bundle at build time.
#
# You do NOT need this file just to run the app — it works out of the box
# against the deployed backend at https://api.goodsolesph.online.

# --- Point Expo Go at your own local backend ---------------------------------
# Uncomment and set to your PC's LAN IP + port when you want to hit a backend
# running on your own machine (for backend changes, database seeding, etc.).
# Find your LAN IP with `ipconfig` on Windows or `ifconfig` on macOS/Linux.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.x:4000

# --- Test AR Try-On over an HTTPS tunnel in dev ------------------------------
# iOS WebView needs HTTPS for camera access, so the AR page (only) loads
# through an ngrok tunnel to the backend. There's a default tunnel URL
# hardcoded in src/api/config.js for testing; set this to override it when
# yours changes. Product images bypass the tunnel entirely — they come from
# Cloudinary directly.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_AR_URL=https://your-tunnel.ngrok-free.dev
